WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.008 --> 00:00:01.800
MARK MIRCHANDANI: In
Google Cloud Platform,

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.428
you'll need a billing account
to pay for any services you use.

00:00:04.428 --> 00:00:06.720
Let's walk through how to
manage and set up permissions

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.033
for a billing account.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.398
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.290
To start, we'll need to go
to the page for the billing

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.040
account.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.590
On the left-hand side,
choose Billing, and then

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:22.930
click on Manage Billing
Accounts to see a list of all

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.280
your billing accounts.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.560
Here, you can see each
billing account, as well as

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.223
the number of projects
associated with each one.

00:00:29.223 --> 00:00:30.640
You can click on
an account to see

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.860
more detailed information
about the account

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.320
and get an overview
of the costs.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.510
To manage this billing
account, click on Manage

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.710
in the top right.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.110
From here, we can see
the associated projects

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:42.850
and manage permissions.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.380
In order to make
sure others can see

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:48.010
costs for this billing account,
let's show how to add a user.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.250
Click Add Member and type
in a user's email address.

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:52.780
Then, choose a role.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.370
The default roles
for billing accounts

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.490
are viewers, users, and admins.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.470
Billing account
viewers have access

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.810
to see the costs associated
with the billing account,

00:01:01.810 --> 00:01:04.209
while users can view
costs and add projects

00:01:04.209 --> 00:01:05.650
to the billing account.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.360
Billing account
administrators can

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.940
do all of that plus manage
the billing account itself,

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.870
such as assigning permissions,
managing export settings,

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.420
or contacting billing support.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.820
For this example, let's add
someone as a billing account

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.550
viewer so that they can see
the costs for this billing

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.950
account and all the
associated projects

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:27.260
without being able to associate
any additional projects.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.440
You can also add a
group and assign roles

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.060
so that all users
in the group will

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.770
share the same permissions.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:37.060
Users and groups can be managed
via G Suite or Cloud Identity.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.190
If you want a user
to only see the costs

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.430
for individual projects rather
than all the costs for projects

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.410
attached to a billing
account, give them

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:46.840
the project viewer
role on each project

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.790
rather than billing account
viewer on the billing account.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:51.490
Similarly for all
permissions, you

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:54.040
can even assign a group
to the project viewer role

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.570
and then add users
to that group.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:59.290
Now, if you're a billing account
user or admin on a billing

00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:01.540
account, you'll be able
to link that billing

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.300
account to a project
when you create it.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.730
If you want to change the
billing account for a project,

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.860
head back to the Billing
Account Management page

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.870
and click on the Options
menu next to that project.

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:15.230
Choose Change Billing and then
pick a new billing account.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.680
You can also disable
billing for a project, which

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.360
will shut down all paid
resources for that project,

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:22.057
so be careful.

00:02:22.057 --> 00:02:24.640
Now, you should be able to start
managing your billing account

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.330
and assigning
permissions to them.

